        <strong>Jardins do Palácio de Cristal</strong>
      </a>
      - A large public garden and park in Porto, known for its beautifully landscaped grounds and sweeping panoramic views over the Douro River. 
      One of the city’s most popular green spaces.
      I only spent about an hour here during a longer walk and immediately wished I had planned more time. 
      The gardens were stunning, the views of Porto’s bridges were spectacular, the peacocks were endlessly entertaining, and the fact that it was all free made it even better. 
      If I were to redo the trip, I would grab lunch from a nearby café or market and have a picnic here. 
      This felt like a true must-see.
