      - A 19th-century building in Porto’s historic center, originally constructed to house the city’s Commercial Association. 
      It served as Porto’s stock exchange and commercial court and is renowned for its lavish interiors, especially the Arab Room inspired by Moorish design. 
      Still used today for official ceremonies, conferences, and cultural events.
      This was one of my favorite visits. 
      The palace is stunning, rich with history, and I was genuinely disappointed when the guided tour ended. 
      I wanted more time to wander the halls, learn about the building's evolving role through time, and better understand the events that took place here. 
      Porto’s seafaring, mercantile, and industrial history all seem to converge in this building. 
      Tours are scheduled in various languages at various times, so make sure to book in advance.
