      - One of the world’s oldest demarcated wine regions and a major wine-producing area in northern Portugal. 
      Tours typically include visits to traditional wine estates, tastings (including Port wine), and scenic views of terraced vineyards along the Douro River.
      This was a long day, about eight hours, but easily the highlight of the trip. 
      The tour was led by a young Porto local trying to establish himself in the tourism industry and he did a phenomenal job.  
      He delivered the whole tour in English and kept the long driving stretches informative and engaging. 
      We traveled far upstream into the mountains and made three stops. 
      The first was a smaller, modern winery focused on organic and efficient production, where we sampled several wines. 
      The second stop involved boarding boats in a small town and cruising past vineyards while enjoying wine onboard. 
      The final stop was at a large, traditional winery, where we were treated to dinner and an impressive selection of wines, including an excellent vintage Port. 
      This was the best experience of the trip.
