  <section class="two-column section-wide">
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Food &amp; Drink</h2>
      <p>
        Meals in Porto are built around fresh, local ingredients and a strong connection to the Atlantic, with seafood, vegetables, fruits, and whole grains forming the backbone of the cuisine, alongside familiar staples like pork, rice, legumes, and potatoes. 
        The city has quietly built a reputation as one of the best places to eat in Portugal.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some of the most enjoyable meals are found in small, family-run restaurants in and around the Ribeira and throughout the old city, where locals eat daily. 
        These places tend to be relaxed, welcoming, and focused on generous portions rather than presentation. 
        Space is often tight, which sometimes means sharing tables, but that only adds to the atmosphere. 
        Ordering the <i>prato do dia</i> (dish of the day) or simply following the waiter’s recommendation is usually the best way to experience a well-prepared, satisfying meal at a reasonable price.
      </p>

      <p>
        Everyday food is just as important here. 
        Porto is filled with bakeries and pastry shops that double as neighborhood cafés, serving inexpensive pastries, espresso, and simple sandwiches.
      </p>

      <p>
        Try a francesinha, ideally somewhere locals actually eat rather than the main riverfront strip. 
        The waterfront is scenic but comes with predictable markups. 
        Port wine is exceptional in Porto, and much of it never leaves Europe. 
        Serious wine enthusiasts are missing out if they skip Porto and the Douro Valley.
      </p>

      <p>
        When I travel, I usually rely on Google Maps to scout restaurants, checking menus and reviews ahead of time. 
        Other times, I decide on the spot, choosing a place simply because the location feels right, the room looks inviting, or the menu catches my eye. 
        Food preferences are deeply subjective, but if you’d like a few recommendations:
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="https://mercadobolhao.pt/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <strong>Mercado do Bolhão</strong>
        </a>
